Z||000000||beachbomb||05-28-2001||03:40 PM||||Hi all, i have been chasing a high idle problem since i bought my indy a year and a half ago, i have replaced or fixed just about everything on it, which did fix the worst of the high idle, but it still idles around 1400 rpm, today i was looking around my engine compartment and noticed a hairline crack on my exhaust manifold, just above the 02 sensor(at the weld joint), could this be the cause?? If so is the a way to fix it without replacing the manifold?..thanks..jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||05-28-2001||08:06 PM||||Yes it can cause problems if it's letting air into the O2 sensor. There is no reliable permanent fix but to replace the manifold.||||reg||1
